    "body": "<p>As of Saturday 22 August, Bitcoin had run from the low sixties to the high seventies in a week. The question in the room was not \u201cis the market interesting.\u201d It was \u201cwhen does this crash.\u201d</p>\n<p>The honest answer is that nobody can date <em>the</em> crash. What the tape usually does is flush when leverage, a thin book, and a dated catalyst overlap. That is a window, not a prophecy.</p>\n<h2>What was live</h2>\n<p>Spot sat near $78,600 with a seven-day range of roughly $62,700 to $79,300 \u2014 about twenty-five percent in a week, and still some thirty-eight percent below the 6 October 2025 high at $126,080. Dominance was still Bitcoin-led. The meme book was already late-beta: dogs and frogs up twenty to thirty-eight percent in a day.</p>\n<h2>The calendar that matters</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>26 August \u2014 Nvidia, and the PCE print</li>\n<li>27\u201329 August \u2014 Jackson Hole; Warsh on the 28th</li>\n<li>16 September \u2014 FOMC</li>\n</ul>\n<p>September seasonality is a small sample. It is not a law. Use the meeting, not the month.</p>\n<h2>The desk plan</h2>\n<p>Observation first. A Daily close back above $80,000 while $70,000 holds is confirmation of continuation. A Daily close below $70,000 is the risk-off line. Chasing $78,000 after a vertical week is not a plan.</p>\n<blockquote>Until confirmation prints, just observe. Cash is a valid state.</blockquote>\n<p>Council weights through 16 September were twenty / fifty / thirty, bull / base / bear. The base case: two-way trade between $70,000 and $82,000, memes giving back a large share of the blow-off, no dated crash.</p>\n<p>This letter is educational scenario research. It is not personalized advice and it does not recommend leverage.</p>\n",
